<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piero Strozzi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–<a href="/years/1558">1558</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piero Strozzi was a Florentine exile and soldier, the son of Filippo Strozzi, who fought against the Medici and became a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He commanded French and Sienese forces in the war for Siena but was defeated by the imperial and Florentine army at Marciano (Scannagallo) in 1554. He was killed at the siege of Thionville in 1558.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piero-strozzi.jpg" alt="Piero Strozzi" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of François Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piero-Strozzi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
